WEBVTT

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.003
Do you know about
Season Fairies?

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.872
They make the rain fall.
They make the wind blow...

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.040
They make clouds.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.532
They're little fairies
who govern the seasons.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.279
But... can you believe it?

00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:16.272
It tumbled into my
room, of all places!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.286
Are you listening
to me, Sugar?

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:21.447
Yeah, I heard you.
Just a little bit.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.027
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:30.230
On my lips

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.030
The rouge of tears

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.991
Sugar Baby Love

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:04.988
I don't want to know
such a thing as love.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.539
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.742
On my lips

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.007
The rouge of tears

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:27.220
On Thursdays

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.223
I buy roses and

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:34.387
add a letter.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:41.535
Sugar Baby Love

00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:44.437
When I see you
in my dreams,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:48.430
you're so caring.

00:01:53.547 --> 00:01:55.708
Good morning, everyone!

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.645
Bringing dreams to
children from town to town,

00:01:58.752 --> 00:02:01.988
we are The Hammond
Theater Troupe.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:07.551
Today we've come to Muhlenburg
on a special provincial tour!

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.197
Tomorrow in
the town's theater

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.257
we will be having a
public performance!

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.971
The musical program you
will be viewing is entitled,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.006
"The Bear Pianist,"

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:25.011
a story guaranteed to have
your heart awash with tears.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:29.471
A fairy tale of love
and deep emotion!

00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:30.817
Waffo!

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.318
We are The Hammond Theater Troupe, and
we've come to Muhlenburg today...

00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:34.020
We are The Hammond Theater Troupe, and
we've come to Muhlenburg today...
What? What?
Hey, what's going on?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.023
...on a special provincial tour.
Tomorrow in the town's theater...

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.626
...on a special provincial tour.
Tomorrow in the town's theater...
What is it?
How did you get this big?

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.827
And here we have...
Was it some kind of spell?

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.028
And here we have...
Hey, hey, hey!

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:43.757
The Forest Fairy.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:45.920
Hello!

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:49.636
And this is the
mysterious boy pianist!

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.127
Hello, everyone!

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:57.644
Come and see it, everyone.
Here you go! Here!

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.946
Come and see it, everyone.
Here you go! Here!

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.648
Such a heart-breaking story.
Come and see it, everyone.
Here you go! Here!

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.983
Such a heart-breaking story.
Here you go!

00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:03.984
Hey, hey, hey,
Forest Fairy!

00:03:03.984 --> 00:03:05.619
Don't forget, everyone.
Hey, hey, hey,
Forest Fairy!

00:03:05.619 --> 00:03:09.316
We'll put a twinkle in your hearts!

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.218
A "Twinkle"?

00:03:24.004 --> 00:03:25.872
What's wrong with Norma?

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.108
It must be this.

00:03:28.108 --> 00:03:29.109
Huh?

00:03:29.109 --> 00:03:32.840
She's been this way since
she got this flyer this morning.

00:03:33.013 --> 00:03:35.081
Grandma said it's
been a long time

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.017
since a theater
troupe came to town.

00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:39.747
It looks interesting.
Should we go?

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:40.787
Yeah.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.923
-Oh, I'm going! Me! Me! Me!

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.026
-All right. Just calm down, Norma.
-Oh, I'm going! Me! Me! Me!

00:03:46.026 --> 00:03:47.926
What about you, Anne?

00:03:48.028 --> 00:03:50.030
-Let's go! Let's go!
-All right, let's go.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.965
Yay! Anne, I love you!

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:52.954
Ok, ok.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.468
Ok, then should we make plans?

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.338
-We've been waiting!
-We've been waiting!

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.907
The participants will be
Norma, of course,

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.308
Anne, of course,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.833
me, of course, and then...

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:05.979
Phil!

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:06.980
Huh?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.279
Hey, do you want to come
with us tomorrow to see a play?

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.748
A play?

00:04:11.885 --> 00:04:13.119
Don't be silly.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.989
We don't have time for
little things like that.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:20.016
We're busy with our
scientific research, right?

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:20.994
Y-Yeah...

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:21.995
Right?

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:22.996
Uh, yeah.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.498
So then we'll use this
for our next experiment.

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:29.127
It seems boys have
their problems, too.

00:04:31.071 --> 00:04:31.765
Oh!

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:36.242
Hey, Greta, we're going
to see a play tomorrow.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.677
Do you want to go with us?

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.412
Oh, Miss Saga,

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:43.983
how plebeian of you to get
excited over a little play like that.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.245
As for me...

00:04:45.719 --> 00:04:48.021
Look! I have tickets to next
summer's performance of the...

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.353
...Guten Morgen Royal Opera Company!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.393
I asked Father to
reserve them for me.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:56.963
Next summer Father
and I are going to see it.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:59.830
Of course, they're "S" seats!

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.302
Greta's not coming.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:05.972
W-Wait 'til I'm finished talking!

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.030
So, what?

00:05:07.474 --> 00:05:09.943
Are you going or not?

00:05:09.943 --> 00:05:10.932
I'm going!

00:05:11.111 --> 00:05:12.879
But don't get me wrong.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.677
It's not that I really want
to see that play or anything.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.619
I just want to see what third
rate is like before I see first rate.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:22.383
That's all! Got it?

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.426
Ok, ok, I get it.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.485
What a pain.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.836
We'll go around once
more this afternoon.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.804
Take care of the
fliers for me, Sam.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.404
Yes, Chairman.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.842
They went inside.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.311
I wonder if there's
a "Twinkle" in there.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.046
Let's take a look.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.070
Waffo!

00:05:53.253 --> 00:05:55.622
Oh, nobody is here.

00:05:55.622 --> 00:05:58.523
I wonder if there's
really a "Twinkle" here...

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.336
What's that?

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.946
A piano-playing bear?

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:32.292
It's true,
I'm telling you.

00:06:32.292 --> 00:06:34.123
It was a bear this big.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:37.363
No one else was there,
and it was playing the piano.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.799
Then the bear went...

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.000
ROAR!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.492
-ROAR! ROAR! ROAR!

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:48.007
You guys went to
the theater, didn't you?

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.008
Theater?

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:52.946
Starting tomorrow there's going
to be a play called "The Bear Pianist."

00:06:52.946 --> 00:06:55.938
You guys must have
seen one of the actors.

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:59.181
Hey, hey!
What's a play?

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:02.585
A play is, well...

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.960
when actors get on stage
and act out various stories.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.825
What are actors?

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.230
What is acting?

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.232
Hmm, how can I explain it?

00:07:12.232 --> 00:07:12.966
Hey, what is it? Huh, Saga, huh?
What's an actor? What's acting? Hey!
Hmm, how can I explain it?

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:14.834
Hey, what is it? Huh, Saga, huh?
What's an actor? What's acting? Hey!

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:19.672
Hey, what is it? Huh, Saga, huh?
What's an actor? What's acting? Hey!
At any rate, it seems to have
nothing to a with a "Twinkle".

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:23.977
Hey, what is it? Huh, Saga, huh?
What's an actor? What's acting? Hey!
Hmph! Then what did he mean when he
said they would put a "Twinkle" in our heart?

00:07:23.977 --> 00:07:26.775
Oh, man!
We've been tricked!

00:07:27.981 --> 00:07:29.448
Welcome.

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.750
Welcome.

00:07:42.996 --> 00:07:45.832
Can I drink coffee here?

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:48.001
Yes. Have a seat.

00:07:48.001 --> 00:07:51.334
Hmm, well, hmm...

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:53.702
Here.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.573
Oh, thanks.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.276
Wow, there are so many. Um...

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.782
-There's supposed to be a play tomorrow.
-Really?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.066
Hey, what's with this guy?

00:08:20.066 --> 00:08:22.000
Hasn't he decided yet?

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:26.331
I can't stand it!
Hurry up and decide!

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:29.309
Yay, Salt's in trouble.
Yay!
What're you doing?

00:08:29.309 --> 00:08:31.573
Yay, Salt's in trouble.
Yay!
Let me go.
I didn't do anything wrong!

00:08:35.148 --> 00:08:37.083
You can do it!

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.618
Just one more!

00:08:38.618 --> 00:08:42.247
One more! One more! One more!

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.758
Oh, have you decided yet?

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:49.250
Huh? Ah, um...

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:50.930
I'm back.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.832
Welcome back.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:54.299
Oh. Welcome.

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:55.896
Thank you.

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:59.372
Saga, you can go home now.

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:01.941
I'll take care of the rest.

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.772
I have ten minutes left.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.945
I haven't cleaned out
the roaster yet, either.

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.936
I can do that tomorrow.

00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:11.479
No, that's the plan for today.

00:09:11.818 --> 00:09:12.580
Besides,

00:09:12.819 --> 00:09:15.288
last time you cleaned up,

00:09:15.288 --> 00:09:17.347
it didn't come out very clean.

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:21.160
I've washed and
dried all the dusters.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.355
Oh, and I replenished
the beans, too.

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:26.366
Oh, have you decided yet?

00:09:26.366 --> 00:09:27.196
Huh?

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:28.259
Uh...

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:31.059
well... the blend.

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.736
Ok, coming right up!

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:04.037
Hey, hey, Saga.

00:10:04.037 --> 00:10:07.407
Let's go see Mr. Bear.
Mr. Bear! Come on!

00:10:07.407 --> 00:10:10.001
Shh! Be quiet.

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:14.147
Hey, Saga,
I'll be quiet.

00:10:14.147 --> 00:10:16.349
I'll be a good girl.

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:18.783
So please, please, Saga.

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:23.990
Thank you for waiting.
Here you are.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.252
Thank you.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.301
Oh, no fair!

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:37.428
I want some, too.

00:10:37.737 --> 00:10:39.295
How does it taste?

00:10:39.539 --> 00:10:41.336
Huh?
Oh, yeah.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:48.147
Yeah, it's not bad... but...

00:10:48.147 --> 00:10:49.048
But?

00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:50.538
It's sort of...

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.250
a little bit stiff-tasting.

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:58.958
Hey, what do you mean "stiff"!

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:00.858
He's a poser.
Hey, what do you mean "stiff"!

00:11:23.483 --> 00:11:25.118
This is ridiculous!
Why do I have to stand in line?

00:11:25.118 --> 00:11:27.987
Isn't it time yet? I'm so excited.
This is ridiculous!
Why do I have to stand in line?

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:28.976
Saga!
This is ridiculous!
Why do I have to stand in line?

00:11:29.889 --> 00:11:31.090
Be good.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.292
I only let you come because
you promised you'd be good.

00:11:33.292 --> 00:11:36.028
Hey, hey, Saga.
Is this a play?

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:38.264
It's not very interesting.

00:11:38.264 --> 00:11:39.999
I'm bored.

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:41.023
Not yet.

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:43.202
We'll be seeing
the play soon.

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:44.726
It's Jan.

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:47.039
What are you doing here?

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:50.031
I-I, nothing really...
I mean...

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:52.377
Let's watch it together.

00:12:02.021 --> 00:12:03.010
Alan!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.125
What are you doing here?

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:09.462
My little brothers wanted to
see it, so I had to bring them.

00:12:09.462 --> 00:12:11.828
Little brothers?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.003
Ooh! They look just
like Alan, don't they!

00:12:17.003 --> 00:12:18.504
What about you, Jan?

00:12:18.504 --> 00:12:19.772
I, well...

00:12:19.772 --> 00:12:22.502
It doesn't matter.
Let's all watch it together.

00:12:22.542 --> 00:12:24.010
These seats are empty,
aren't they?

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.877
By the way,
what about Phil?

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:34.477
Hmm, Alan and Jan
sure are late.

00:12:36.022 --> 00:12:38.558
Ooh, it's about to start.

00:12:38.558 --> 00:12:40.593
It's so exciting, isn't it?

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:42.026
How childish,

00:12:42.195 --> 00:12:45.031
getting all excited
about a little play.

00:12:45.031 --> 00:12:47.800
Hey, your elbow's
touching me!

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.563
Move over.

00:12:50.236 --> 00:12:51.971
Be quiet!

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:52.972
Ok!

00:12:52.972 --> 00:12:54.974
Thank you all for coming to see The Hammond
Theater Troupe's special performance today.

00:12:54.974 --> 00:12:57.310
Thank you all for coming to see The Hammond
Theater Troupe's special performance today.
Wh-What! It got all dark!

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:59.779
Thank you all for coming to see The Hammond
Theater Troupe's special performance today.
I can't see anything, Saga!

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:01.714
They will now perform "The Bear Pianist."
Hey, be quiet!

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:02.976
They will now perform "The Bear Pianist."

00:13:07.553 --> 00:13:10.989
Grandma, what is that piano sound?

00:13:11.591 --> 00:13:15.027
The Bear Pianist is playing.

00:13:15.328 --> 00:13:17.353
Bear Pianist?

00:13:17.997 --> 00:13:19.988
Yes. That was...

00:13:32.745 --> 00:13:34.440
I'm so lonely...

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:38.010
Won't anyone be my friend?

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:44.023
Saga! That's him!
The bear from yesterday!

00:13:44.023 --> 00:13:45.149
Shh! Be quiet.

00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:50.129
Oh, my!
There's a bear playing the piano.

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:51.430
How unusual.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:54.967
It's sure to make
a good exhibit!

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:56.369
Oh, it's him!

00:13:56.369 --> 00:13:58.037
The "Twinkle" guy
from yesterday!

00:13:58.037 --> 00:13:59.265
Hey, bear!

00:13:59.739 --> 00:14:01.774
You're going to
come with me.

00:14:01.774 --> 00:14:03.976
You'll make lots of friends.

00:14:03.976 --> 00:14:04.704
Really?

00:14:05.077 --> 00:14:06.806
Will I really make friends?

00:14:07.313 --> 00:14:09.849
Yes, really!

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:11.917
Yay, I'll go!

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:15.755
Friends! Friends! Yay!

00:14:15.755 --> 00:14:17.690
That went well.
Yay, I'll go!
Friends! Friends! Yay!

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:21.717
This will make me rich.
Yay, I'll go!
Friends! Friends! Yay!

00:14:23.296 --> 00:14:24.764
Oh, the bear!

00:14:24.764 --> 00:14:26.699
He's a bad guy!
I knew it!

00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:30.002
He tricked the bear by
saying he'd make friends.

00:14:30.002 --> 00:14:33.806
He tricked us yesterday, too,
saying he'd give us a "Twinkle".

00:14:33.806 --> 00:14:35.308
Ok, let's save the bear!

00:14:35.308 --> 00:14:37.003
Be quiet!

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:43.649
Now bear witness to one of the
wonders of the world: A bear pianist!

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:45.751
Pay on your way out,

00:14:45.751 --> 00:14:48.811
but first take a look!

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.259
This wasn't
supposed to happen...

00:14:53.259 --> 00:14:55.955
I just wanted some friends...

00:14:57.663 --> 00:14:59.961
Oh, what a beauty!

00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:03.968
Will you be friends with me?

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:09.975
Now for one of the wonders
of the world: A bear pianist!

00:15:09.975 --> 00:15:11.977
Pay on your way out.

00:15:11.977 --> 00:15:13.979
Oh, no farther!

00:15:13.979 --> 00:15:17.710
Although it plays the piano, a bear is
still a bear. Any closer is dangerous!

00:15:17.983 --> 00:15:19.618
No, that's not true!

00:15:19.618 --> 00:15:21.987
I just want to
be your friend!

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:22.976
Hey!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.784
You can't just stop!

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:28.551
Play the piano!
The piano!

00:15:28.994 --> 00:15:30.393
How sad.

00:15:31.864 --> 00:15:35.501
A bear is exploited, yet falls
in love with a human girl.

00:15:35.501 --> 00:15:37.662
What an obvious development!

00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:41.474
It's just as I thought.

00:15:41.474 --> 00:15:45.001
No one wants to be
friends with a bear like me.

00:15:45.644 --> 00:15:49.307
Oh, how wonderful it would be
if only I could become human...

00:15:49.849 --> 00:15:52.374
You want to be
human that badly?

00:15:53.753 --> 00:15:55.454
If that's what
you really want,

00:15:55.454 --> 00:15:57.115
I'll grant it...

00:16:05.798 --> 00:16:07.800
Good evening, bear pianist.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:08.801
Who are you?

00:16:08.801 --> 00:16:11.971
I'm a fairy who
grants beautiful wishes.

00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:14.974
I'll grant that beautiful wish of yours.
Oh, it's the fairy from yesterday!

00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:16.965
I'll grant that beautiful wish of yours.
But why is she so big?

00:16:31.791 --> 00:16:32.985
Wh-What happened?

00:16:33.225 --> 00:16:34.988
Please go wherever you wish.

00:16:35.361 --> 00:16:38.387
But you can only remain
in human form at night.

00:16:38.864 --> 00:16:42.129
When dawn comes,
you must return to your cage.

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:48.003
Oh, this loneliness...

00:16:48.374 --> 00:16:51.944
Though it may disappear in
the daytime, when night comes...

00:16:51.944 --> 00:16:54.947
...it feels as though this
small heart will be torn apart.

00:16:54.947 --> 00:16:57.939
Dear Lord...
What can I do?

00:16:59.185 --> 00:17:02.245
Oh...
What beautiful music...

00:17:05.925 --> 00:17:09.952
If only I might dispel
your loneliness at night...

00:17:10.963 --> 00:17:11.964
Thank you.

00:17:11.964 --> 00:17:14.967
Your piano playing is
a light in my heart.

00:17:14.967 --> 00:17:17.236
It always brightens my heart

00:17:17.236 --> 00:17:19.500
as I wander in the darkness.

00:17:20.473 --> 00:17:22.964
Today I have
something to tell you...

00:17:23.442 --> 00:17:24.704
What is it?

00:17:24.844 --> 00:17:27.713
I... I have always...

00:17:27.713 --> 00:17:28.975
Oh, my dear!

00:17:29.315 --> 00:17:30.983
Wherefore art thou,
my beloved!

00:17:30.983 --> 00:17:33.952
Oh, my dear!
There you are!

00:17:33.986 --> 00:17:34.975
Dear!

00:17:41.694 --> 00:17:43.629
Oh... Let me introduce you.

00:17:43.629 --> 00:17:45.187
This is my fiancé.

00:17:45.698 --> 00:17:48.223
He's just returned
from a long journey!

00:17:49.235 --> 00:17:50.224
N-No way!

00:17:51.537 --> 00:17:52.805
Who are you!

00:17:52.805 --> 00:17:54.306
Dear, it's not like that!

00:17:54.306 --> 00:17:57.843
This kind man encouraged
me with his piano playing

00:17:57.843 --> 00:18:01.006
while I awaited your return.

00:18:01.213 --> 00:18:03.807
Oh, please forgive me.

00:18:04.216 --> 00:18:06.707
You must play
at our wedding!

00:18:06.986 --> 00:18:09.352
Regrettably,
I am unable to do so.

00:18:09.722 --> 00:18:10.984
Oh, why not?

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:14.948
I can only stay in this
human form at night.

00:18:15.628 --> 00:18:18.392
When morning comes,
I turn back into a bear.

00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:21.426
What a pleasant fellow!

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:30.476
Now bear witness to one of the
wonders of the world: A bear pianist!

00:18:30.476 --> 00:18:31.977
Pay on your way out,
but first take a look.

00:18:31.977 --> 00:18:35.970
Today is her wedding ceremony.
I wonder what she's doing now.
Pay on your way out,
but first take a look.

00:18:36.615 --> 00:18:37.980
I want to see her.

00:18:38.384 --> 00:18:39.976
Even if it's just a glimpse!

00:18:46.458 --> 00:18:47.720
Get out of my way!

00:18:47.927 --> 00:18:49.261
Let me go!

00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:50.819
I want to see her!

00:18:52.565 --> 00:18:56.126
This is dangerous!
You leave me no choice!

00:18:57.803 --> 00:18:59.464
I want to see her!

00:19:40.446 --> 00:19:42.971
Oh, this song is...

00:19:45.217 --> 00:19:50.553
If only I might dispel
your loneliness at night...

00:19:50.823 --> 00:19:52.984
It was you, wasn't it?

00:20:04.003 --> 00:20:06.267
Thank you, Bear...

00:20:17.516 --> 00:20:19.818
Oh, that was good!

00:20:19.818 --> 00:20:23.055
I cried. Plays are
wonderful, aren't they?

00:20:23.055 --> 00:20:24.556
Especially when the bear
transformed. He was just... ooh!

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:27.491
Especially when the bear
transformed. He was just... ooh!
So, this is a play.
What do you think?

00:20:27.993 --> 00:20:29.895
Did Mr. Bear die?

00:20:29.895 --> 00:20:31.030
Huh, Saga?

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:35.034
It's too much!
He was such a nice bear!

00:20:35.034 --> 00:20:36.502
I-I won't forgive him.

00:20:36.502 --> 00:20:38.663
I'll never forgive that evildoer!

00:20:39.004 --> 00:20:41.768
I told you,
this is just a play.

00:20:43.275 --> 00:20:44.510
Greta...

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.711
W-What?

00:20:45.711 --> 00:20:48.681
I'm telling you, Saga,
I'm not crying.

00:20:48.681 --> 00:20:53.185
I'm not moved. It's dust. Dust!
I got dust in my eye. That's all!

00:20:53.185 --> 00:20:54.420
Hey, Greta.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.821
What?

00:20:55.821 --> 00:20:56.981
Bear.

00:20:57.389 --> 00:20:58.481
Piano.

00:20:58.991 --> 00:20:59.980
Heaven.

00:21:01.393 --> 00:21:02.995
It sure looks like
she's moved.

00:21:02.995 --> 00:21:04.394
I know.

00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:16.141
What?

00:21:16.141 --> 00:21:19.872
Why are they being
nice to that evildoer?

00:21:24.016 --> 00:21:24.950
Mr. Bear!

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.008
Waffo!

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.420
Mr. Bear, you're all right!

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:39.691
Oh, it's the guy
from yesterday!

00:21:45.838 --> 00:21:48.040
Hey, Saga?
Why? Why?

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:50.042
Why was Mr. Bear alive?

00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:52.978
Why is he that strange
guy from yesterday?

00:21:52.978 --> 00:21:54.969
You're too noisy!

00:21:55.547 --> 00:21:59.118
What? Why can't you just tell me?
Meanie Saga!

00:21:59.118 --> 00:22:01.186
Meanie, meanie, meanie Saga!

00:22:01.186 --> 00:22:03.856
I had no idea he was the bear...

00:22:03.856 --> 00:22:04.990
What is it, Saga?
Are you listening?

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:08.687
What is it, Saga?
Are you listening?
It's just, ooh...

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:25.778
Wishes upon the Moon

00:22:25.778 --> 00:22:29.014
Melting in the water

00:22:29.014 --> 00:22:34.620
I found a street lined with trees

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:38.522
Songs of stardust

00:22:39.358 --> 00:22:47.733
The breeze crossing over
the Bridge of Rainbows

00:22:47.733 --> 00:22:52.871
You already knew...

00:22:52.871 --> 00:22:57.976
the happiness of
connecting our hearts

00:22:57.976 --> 00:23:00.078
Sugar Snow

00:23:00.078 --> 00:23:07.986
When powdery snow whirls in town

00:23:07.986 --> 00:23:12.991
the season of flower
blossoms is near...

00:23:12.991 --> 00:23:17.724
and, I think of you.

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:26.004
The love that melts
our hearts and...

00:23:26.004 --> 00:23:34.002
the dreams are in your heart

00:23:39.818 --> 00:23:40.886
Preview of Next Episode

00:23:40.886 --> 00:23:44.423
Preview of Next Episode
Waffo! Mr. Bear was a good
piano player. Right, Saga?

00:23:44.423 --> 00:23:46.258
I told you it wasn't real.

00:23:46.258 --> 00:23:48.861
It was just a costume.
Vincent was inside!

00:23:48.861 --> 00:23:51.430
What? A costume
can play the piano?

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:52.965
I wonder how it moves.

00:23:52.965 --> 00:23:54.433
Is it a spell after all?

00:23:54.433 --> 00:23:56.235
Hmm... Plays are strange.

00:23:56.235 --> 00:23:58.971
I don't think a Season Fairy
can talk about strange...

00:23:58.971 --> 00:24:02.975
"A Little Snow Fairy Sugar"
The Next Episode Is
"A Backstage Happening."

00:24:02.975 --> 00:24:06.467
What did you mean
by stiff-tasting?
